## Output Format
Return a JSON array of test cases. Each test case must have:
- "id": unique test case ID (e.g., "TC-001")
- "title": concise test case title
- "description": what this test case verifies
- "endpoint": "METHOD /path" (the target endpoint)
- "test_type": one of "functional", "boundary", "negative", "performance", "security", "integration"
- "priority": one of "high", "medium", "low"
- "preconditions": array of setup steps
- "steps": array of test execution steps
- "expected_results": array of expected outcomes
- "tags": array of labels (e.g., "smoke", "regression", "auth", "crud", "boundary", "security", "performance")

## Quality Checklist (must follow)
1. **Endpoint accuracy**: the "endpoint" field must EXACTLY match one of the API Endpoints above ("METHOD /path"). Never invent or mismatch endpoints. Every step that calls an API must use the same endpoint as the "endpoint" field.
2. **CRUD completeness**: for every resource, cover Create, Read, Update, Delete when the spec exposes them. Never omit an existing operation (e.g., missing PUT/PATCH update cases).
3. **Assertability**: every expected_result must be machine-checkable: explicit HTTP status code, and specific field value or field presence/absence (e.g., "Response body does NOT contain the password field").
4. **Boundary values**: test min/max lengths, pagination limit maximum, field case-sensitivity, empty strings.
5. **Security**: SQL injection / XSS payloads, rate limiting, token expiry & refresh, IDOR (horizontal authorization), password strength policy.
6. **Performance**: response time baseline (e.g., P95 < 200ms), concurrency/throughput for key endpoints.
7. **Cleanup & idempotency**: include teardown/cleanup in preconditions for created data; cover duplicate/repeated submissions.
8. **I18N**: cover unicode / emoji / whitespace / special characters in text fields.

